<title>GERMANY: Siemens, Westinghouse seen in power tie.</title>
<headline>Siemens, Westinghouse seen in power tie.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Siemens AG's KWU power-generation unit plans to combine its fossil-fuel power operations in a joint venture with Westinghouse, industry sources said.</p>
<p>The merger is likely to be completed this year, and the new company will probably have its headquarters in the United States, one source said.</p>
<p>A KWU spokesman declined to comment on the merger, saying the company does not comment on rumours.</p>
<p>Alfons Graf, head of the Siemens works council and deputy chairman of the supervisory board, confirmed that talks were being held with Westinghouse, as well as with others.</p>
<p>&quot;Siemens must change,&quot; Graf told Reuters.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
